Build the engine as a static library.

Not an upstream bug — a deliberate divergence, so it is a patch of its own with a
different lifetime from 001. Upstream declares `onnxruntime-genai` `SHARED`
unconditionally and has no static option.

A static engine links into the app binary: no framework to embed beside the
llama.cpp ones, no dylib to codesign, and nothing extra for the unsigned CI archive
to carry.

Two consequences the build script handles rather than this patch:

  - A static target propagates its link interface, so `install(EXPORT …)` fails on
    `ortcustomops` and the telemetry target not being in the export set. The script
    configures with `CMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_RULES=ON`; nothing installs from this tree.
  - The archive is only the engine's own objects, so the script combines it with
    `ortcustomops`, `ocos_operators` and `noexcep_operators` through `libtool`, the
    way `build-llama.sh` combines ggml's.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -112,7 +112,7 @@
   endif()
   set(ORTGENAI_COMPILE_TARGET onnxruntime-genai)
   set(ORTGENAI_USAGE_SCOPE PRIVATE)
-  add_library(onnxruntime-genai SHARED ${generator_srcs})
+  add_library(onnxruntime-genai STATIC ${generator_srcs})
 else()
   set(ORTGENAI_COMPILE_TARGET onnxruntime-genai-obj)
   set(ORTGENAI_USAGE_SCOPE PUBLIC)
